WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.583
Separate essential work. The event page needs correct booking information, but recommendations are optional. Give these paths different deadlines and resource budgets.

2
00:00:36.583 --> 00:01:12.000
An optional call stalls. Recommendations stop responding. Without a boundary, waiting calls can consume all connections or workers and affect otherwise healthy operations.

3
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Enforce a deadline. The timeout guard ends waiting for optional work. This protects local resources but does not prove a remote write was cancelled or never happened.

4
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:34.750
Degrade honestly. Render the essential page without suggestions. Do not turn an uncertain payment outcome into a success message just to make the page appear healthy.

5
00:02:34.750 --> 00:03:07.500
Bound retries. If a retry is appropriate, limit attempts and use backoff with jitter. Preserve one operation identity for side effects so retries do not create duplicate business actions.

6
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:53.750
Test partial failure. Inject a slow response and a lost reply in a safe test environment. Verify core capacity and user-visible correctness rather than only testing a clean server shutdown.
